# NOTE: This package is intentionally omitted from the build.
#
# kortex_driver links against Kinova's Kortex API, a closed-source, prebuilt
# binary SDK that upstream's CMakeLists.txt downloads at configure time
# (artifactory.kinovaapps.com/.../kortex/API/2.5.0/linux_x86-64_x86_gcc.zip).
# There is no source to build it from, and the SDK is only distributed as a
# GCC (libstdc++) build, which is ABI-incompatible with this registry's
# hermetic LLVM/libc++ toolchain since the Kortex C++ API passes std::string,
# std::vector, std::function, etc. across its boundary. Every target
# below is therefore commented out so that `bazel build //...`-style
# patterns over the full distribution do not attempt to build it.
#
# The original rules are preserved verbatim (commented) so they can be
# restored if a libc++-compatible Kortex API ever becomes available.

